BUILD_ONLY: ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/efe-private:quadrotor-landing-<images/quadrotor-landing/VERSION> (the roboEngineer Neural Landing
evaluator) is never published (docs/protocol/README.md §1). An evaluation host builds it (prepare_assets.sh, then
`docker build -f images/quadrotor-landing/Dockerfile .` from the repository root), or takes it from the organization's own
non-public copy of the package.

Why
  It holds the residual force network converted from the Neural Lander release checkpoint
  (github GuanyaShi/neural_lander_sim_1d, pinned commit; images/quadrotor-landing/prepare_assets.py), a repository with
  no licence: it may not be redistributed. The conversion is byte-reproducible (the Dockerfile checks its digest).
  The agent's image is built by each task from the shared client base and holds none of it.
